.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH batten-task 1  batten 
.SH NAME
batten\-task \- What long\-running tasks are doing, recorded where it can be read without a log
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbatten task\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
What long\-running tasks are doing, recorded where it can be read without a log
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
batten\-task\-register(1)
Record that a task has started, under its pid
.TP
batten\-task\-phase(1)
Record what a registered task is now doing
.TP
batten\-task\-tick(1)
Record that a task\*(Aqs loop went round
.TP
batten\-task\-sig(1)
Record that the world a task is watching moved
.TP
batten\-task\-unregister(1)
Drop a task\*(Aqs record, which its exit path does and a kill cannot
.TP
batten\-task\-read(1)
One field of one task\*(Aqs record, so a prober composes rather than parsing the layout
.TP
batten\-task\-alive(1)
What tasks are running right now and what phase each is in — one call, no log reading
.TP
batten\-task\-help(1)
Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)
